Subject: LinkageChecker: shared cache check without Fiddle

dyld keeps system dylibs only in its shared cache, so a missing /usr/lib path is checked with
_dyld_shared_cache_contains_path through Fiddle. A program that cannot call C functions (rb2go has no cgo:
Fiddle.dlopen raises Fiddle::DLError) falls back to the paths the shared cache holds.
---
diff --git a/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/mac/linkage_checker.rb b/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/mac/linkage_checker.rb
index ad71b52f2d..bc0e6d89eb 100644
--- a/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/mac/linkage_checker.rb
+++ b/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/mac/linkage_checker.rb
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@ module OS
       def dylib_found_in_shared_cache?(dylib)
         require "os/mac/ffi"
         MacOS::FFI.dyld_shared_cache_contains_path(dylib)
+      rescue Fiddle::DLError
+        # Without a C function call (a compiled brew) only system paths are in the shared cache.
+        dylib.start_with?("/usr/lib/", "/System/Library/")
       end
     end
   end
